{"name":"Alexandria","hex":"#ff8f73","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Alexandria","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city, port, and former capital of Egypt famed for its ancient library and lighthouse.","Various other former cities in West Asia founded by Alexander the Great, including"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Alexandria"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alexandria","blocks":[{"text":"Alexandria is a major city in Egypt. Lying at the western edge of the Nile River Delta, it extends about 40 km (25 mi) along the country's northern coast. It is Egypt's principal seaport, the second largest city after Cairo, and the largest city on the Mediterranean coast. Founded in 331 BC by Alexander the Great, Alexandria was one of the largest and most important cities of antiquity and a leading hub for science, culture, and scholarship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG/330px-San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandria","wikidata":"Q87"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG/500px-San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG/1280px-San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG/500px-San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASan_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Alexandria_Egypt_%28235108285%29.jpeg/500px-Alexandria_Egypt_%28235108285%29.jpeg